blocks.en:
Our contributions are:
(1) Live: a reusable collection protocol and pipeline , which records search results while questions are unresolved and demonstrates leakage under the tested post-hoc date filters;
(2) Controlled: an evaluation protocol on fixed evidence , which separates model comparison from evidence acquisition and establishes model and market baselines;
(3) Replayable: recorded evidence trajectories and sequential replay , which support controlled memory experiments and show that memory mainly steadies forecasts;
and (4) Source-Aware: a controlled comparison of four commercial search APIs , showing that source differences can exceed model differences in accuracy.

